# SEO parity standards

These patterns were established to bring GoEasyTools to parity with the highest-performing sister site (Astra). Follow them for all new pages and tools.

## Structured data (root layout)

Root `app/layout.tsx` emits three global JSON-LD schemas:
- **WebSite** with site name, URL, description
- **Organization** with logo
- **SoftwareApplication** with `featureList` (12 categories) and `aggregateRating`

Homepage `app/page.tsx` emits **ItemList** JSON-LD listing all tools.

Per-tool pages via `components/tool-page.tsx` emit:
- **WebApplication** with `isAccessibleForFree: true`
- **BreadcrumbList** (Home → category → tool)
- **FAQPage** when FAQs exist in `lib/faqs.ts`
- **HowTo** when steps exist in `lib/how-tos.ts`

When adding a new tool: add FAQs in `lib/faqs.ts` AND HowTo steps in `lib/how-tos.ts`.

## Hreflang

`lib/seo.ts` → `toolMetadata()` passes `tool.id` as `pageId` to enable hreflang links. Never remove this. When adding a new tool, its `id` automatically becomes an `IndexableId` eligible for hreflang.

## Server-rendered locale `lang`

`middleware.ts` detects locale from URL prefix and sets `x-locale` header. Root layout reads this header to set `<html lang>` server-side. Do NOT use client-side `useEffect` to set `lang` — crawlers won't see it.

## Content depth requirements

Every tool page MUST have:
1. A dedicated `components/{tool}-guide.tsx` with **60+ lines** of educational content
2. At minimum: "How it works", "Common use cases", "Tips & best practices", "Privacy" sections
3. Content must be specific to the tool — no generic filler

Do NOT put inline content directly in `page.tsx` for new tools. Always create a guide component.

Do NOT include internal roadmap text like "Demand for this tool is not yet validated" in indexable HTML.

## Guide hub pages

`app/guides/[slug]/page.tsx` serves 9 programmatic category guide pages from `lib/guide-content.ts`. Each guide has:
- SEO-optimized title and description
- 200+ word educational intro
- 3-4 topical sections
- FAQPage + BreadcrumbList JSON-LD
- Tools grid for the category
- Cross-links to related guides

When adding a new tool category, add a matching guide in `lib/guide-content.ts`.

## Blog

Blog posts live in `lib/blog.ts`. Each post must:
- Target a specific long-tail search query
- Be 800-1200 words of genuinely educational content
- Link to 2-3 relevant tools
- Include a FAQ section
- Have unique title and meta description

## googleBot directives

Root metadata includes `googleBot` with `max-image-preview: "large"` and `max-snippet: -1`. Do not weaken these.

## Security headers

`next.config.ts` sets CSP, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy, X-Frame-Options, Permissions-Policy, and `poweredByHeader: false`. Maintain these on all responses.
